  "worked_solution": "The multiples of $10$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={10,20,30,40,\u2026}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,\u2026}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B\u2216A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $10,20,30,40,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $10$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\u2216A & =B-A \\\\  & ={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,\u2026}-{10,20,30,40,\u2026} \\\\  & ={5,15,25,35,\u2026}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
